  "answer": "SQLite’s official [Transaction documentation](https://www.sqlite.org/lang_transaction.html) explains transaction control:\n\n- **`BEGIN`** starts an explicit transaction, grouping subsequent operations until `COMMIT` or `ROLLBACK`. The default is `BEGIN DEFERRED`, which delays starting the database transaction until the first database access.\n- **`COMMIT`** saves the transaction’s changes and ends it. `END TRANSACTION` is an alias.\n- **`ROLLBACK`** undoes the transaction’s uncommitted changes and ends it.\n\nSee also the official [Savepoints documentation](https://www.sqlite.org/lang_savepoint.html), which clarifies that plain `COMMIT` and `ROLLBACK` apply to the entire transaction.",
